      "name": "history-0-typed",
      "question": "Why?",
      "recognizedQuestion": "Why?",
      "answer": "CUDA groups 32 threads into a warp so the GPU can schedule them together and efficiently execute the same instruction across multiple data values. If threads take different branches, each path runs with only its participating lanes active, because the warp cannot execute two different instructions simultaneously. The number 32 is NVIDIA’s architectural choice, not a fundamental requirement of parallel computing.",
